# son-puz.lic -- Sonreeva puzzles, one at a time
# Works out which Sonreeva room you're in (from its title and description), does the puzzle
# there that your 10/25-10/26 runs solved, walks you to the next spot, and exits. Run it
# again at the next puzzle. It never fights and never pays unless you say so.
#
#   ;son-puz         do the next puzzle from where you stand
#   ;son-puz pay     same, and at the Mausoleum it also gets you past the justicar and rides the
#                    chute down: a plain OFFER first (enough once you've paid for this run), then
#                    OFFER 15000 soul shards twice if that didn't do it. Without `pay` it only says so
#   ;son-puz         while you are sliding down the chute (any time, even if you just started
#                    sliding): leans right/left at each "faint light" line until you are spat out
#   ;son-puz summon  in the Den of the Fiend with no fiend about: touches the runes twice to call
#                    it (Nety's words; the verb is a guess). It never fights.
#
# Where it works (everything below was read out of your logs):
#   Graveyard Temporalis, at the mausoleum   go black mausoleum
#   Mausoleum                                ask justicar about entry, OFFER (plain, then 15000
#                                            twice; only with `pay`), then the chute: "faint light coming from the
#                                            right/left" -> LEAN RIGHT/LEFT, "straight ahead"
#                                            -> nothing, until you "spit out onto the ground"
#   the loop of colored rooms (arrival crypt, blue/yellow/red/green rooms): walks to the Dead
#                                            End, touches blue, yellow, violet, orange, red,
#                                            green runes 3 s apart, and goes through the
#                                            narrow opening (it stays open only ~60 s) to the
#                                            Hall of the Dead
#   Hall of the Dead x2                      north, north, to the Dais
#   Dais / Grand Hall (north room)           LOOK DOOR names the item shape ("an empty
#                                            depression in the shape of a fang"); it gets that
#                                            item from your containers, PUTs it in the door and
#                                            goes through. The item is used up, and the drops
#                                            (fang, caduceus ...) come from the creatures
#   Grand Hall (first room)                  JUMP TRAPDOOR over and over until it gives way and dumps you
#                                            into the Subterrane (the north room's caduceus door only
#                                            leads to the Courtyard, a side room, so from that room it
#                                            walks you back south to the trapdoor)
#
# Everything from here on was read out of the 10/26 run with Nety's group. [typed] = you typed it
# in that log, [text] = the game text was in the log but someone else did it, [map] = only the Lich
# map has the command. It stops at each point where the group should be together.
#   Subterrane                               GO FISSURE [map], then north x4 along the Dark Passageway
#   Dead End (the abyss edge)                JUMP [typed] into the Void, a safe room where groups wait
#   The Void                                 CRAWL CREVICE [typed] (a SEARCH first if it isn't there),
#                                            then down x7 the Collapsed Tunnel [map] to the Cistern
#   Cistern                                  SWIM [typed]: drops through a hatch that locks behind you
#   Sunken Chamber                           south, then down x4 / north x5 to the Demon Wall [text]
#   Demon Wall                               the monolithic stone door wants an ouroboros (door routine)
#   Hollowlair, Dreadgrounds                 a shifting maze it can't solve; in the room with "the heavily
#                                            carved door" it WHISPERs "door six" [typed], which sends you
#                                            alone to the Dark Sanctuary
#   Dark Sanctuary                           north to the Dark Shrine (the wall and pit are an optional
#                                            blessing)
#   Dark Shrine                              GO GATE up to 3 times [map]; the third knock strangles whoever
#                                            opens it [text]
#   Den of the Fiend                         SEARCH the dead fiend for the shadowglass effigy, then the door
#                                            routine (the effigy opens the barbed stone door; it slams shut
#                                            about a minute later)
#   Demon Roost (safe room)                  GO GAP, up, GO TUNNEL [typed], north x2, up x2 the Bone Church
#                                            to the Tower
#   Tower                                    GO PORTAL once the rune ring is disarmed (a rogue's job)
#   the ash field                            GO PATH, then run me again within 30 s to confirm [typed]: the
#                                            point of no return
#   the pool (boss room)                     LOOK IN POOL for the gateway, put the soulstone heart in it,
#                                            GO GATEWAY. The boss fight is yours.
#   The Veil of Solace                       the monstrosity: your reward pick is permanent, so no auto-pick
#
# Everything lives in the module: top-level defs/constants are shared by every Lich script.

module SonPuz
  RUNES     = %w[blue yellow violet orange red green].freeze
  RUNE_GAP  = 3       # seconds between touches (Tarakan's group and yours used 3-6)
  OPENING   = /northern wall begins to rumble/i
  # the chute has no room of its own, and its lines carry on after you start ;son-puz (10.26: it
  # said "at loop" mid-slide because the title was already the crypt's), so the text decides
  CHUTE_START = /ushers you into a chute|You are sliding downward/i
  CHUTE_LINES = /sliding downward|slide downward, picking up speed|faint light coming|keep sliding downward|missing your opportunity to navigate|spit out onto the ground/i
  CHUTE_END   = /spit out onto the ground/i
  OFFER_STOP  = /not enough|don't have|cannot afford|can't afford/i
  GAVE_WAY    = /causing it to give way and dump you into the darkness|give way and dump you/i
  DOOR_OPENS  = /causing the .*(?:door|gateway) to open/i
  # the Bone Church on the way to the tower: the step to take in each room
  CHURCH_STEP = [[/Narthex|Nave/i, 'north'], [/Altar/i, 'up'], [/Tower Approach/i, 'up']].freeze
  # loop room (by what its description says) => the step toward the Dead End
  LOOP_STEP = [
    [/Several torches are affixed upon the granite walls/i, 'northeast'],   # arrival crypt
    [/glowing blue mark/i,                                  'north'],
    [/faint yellow sigil/i,                                 'northwest'],
    [/red symbol painted onto the center altar/i,           'northeast'],
    [/barely covering a green marking/i,                    'north']
  ].freeze

  def self.say(msg)
    echo "[son-puz] #{msg}"
  end

  def self.title;  XMLData.room_title.to_s;       end
  def self.descr;  XMLData.room_description.to_s; end

  # => a symbol naming the spot, or nil
  def self.where
    t, d = title, descr
    if    t =~ /Graveyard Temporalis/i && d =~ /black marble mausoleum/i then :mausoleum_door
    elsif t =~ /Sonreeva, Mausoleum/i             then :mausoleum
    elsif t =~ /Sonreeva, Dead End/i              then(d =~ /abyss/i ? :abyss_edge : :dead_end)
    elsif t =~ /Sonreeva, Hall of the Dead/i      then :hall
    elsif t =~ /Sonreeva, Dais/i                  then :dais
    elsif t =~ /Sonreeva, Grand Hall/i            then(d =~ /trapdoor/i ? :grand_first : :grand_door)
    elsif t =~ /Sonreeva, Courtyard/i             then :courtyard
    elsif t =~ /Sonreeva, (?:Crypt|Voln Encampment)/i then :loop
    elsif t =~ /Sonreeva, Subterrane/i            then :subterrane
    elsif t =~ /Sonreeva, Dark Passageway/i       then :passage
    elsif t =~ /Sonreeva, The Void/i              then :void
    elsif t =~ /Sonreeva, Collapsed Tunnel/i      then :tunnel
    elsif t =~ /Sonreeva, Cistern/i               then :cistern
    elsif t =~ /Sonreeva, Sunken Chamber/i        then :sunken
    elsif t =~ /Sonreeva, (?:Depths|Deepest Parts|Palisade)/i then :depths
    elsif t =~ /Sonreeva, Demon Wall/i            then :demon_wall
    elsif t =~ /Hollowlair, Dreadgrounds/i        then :dreadgrounds
    elsif t =~ /Hollowlair, Dark Sanctuary/i      then :sanctuary
    elsif t =~ /Hollowlair, Dark Shrine/i         then :shrine
    elsif t =~ /Hollowlair, Den of the Fiend/i    then :den
    elsif t =~ /Hollowlair, Demon Roost/i         then :roost
    elsif t =~ /Hollowlair, Hellscape/i           then(d =~ /gap leads back/i ? :hellscape_low : :hellscape_high)
    elsif t =~ /The Bone Church, Tower\b(?! Approach)/i then :tower
    elsif t =~ /The Bone Church/i                 then :church
    elsif t =~ /The Veil of Solace/i              then :veil
    # these two have no title in the log (Lich's header is blank), so the description decides
    elsif d =~ /pale, ash-covered earth/i         then :field
    elsif d =~ /pool of stagnant water/i          then :boss_pool
    end
  end

  def self.exits; Array(XMLData.room_exits).map(&:to_s); end

  # Send a command and wait for the room to change (title or description), up to secs.
  # @return true if it did
  def self.step(cmd, secs = 6)
    before = [title, descr]
    waitrt?
    fput "stand" unless standing?       # falls and crawls (trapdoor, abyss, crevice) leave you down
    fput cmd
    deadline = Time.now + secs
    sleep 0.2 until [title, descr] != before || Time.now > deadline
    [title, descr] != before
  end

  # ---- stages ------------------------------------------------------------

  def self.at_mausoleum_door
    say "going into the mausoleum."
    say "didn't get in." unless step("go black mausoleum")
  end

  # Plain OFFER first: on 10/26 19:00:12 an already-paid run was ushered into the chute by a plain
  # `offer`. If that does nothing, the full price (15,000 soul shards) is offered twice.
  def self.at_mausoleum(pay)
    unless pay
      say "this is the Mausoleum. `;son-puz pay` asks the justicar for entry and OFFERs (plain, then 15,000 soul shards twice), then rides the chute."
      return
    end
    waitrt?
    fput "ask justicar about entry"
    sleep 1
    r = ""
    ["offer", "offer 15000", "offer 15000"].each do |cmd|
      r = dothistimeout(cmd, 5, Regexp.union(CHUTE_START, /OFFER again within 30 seconds/i, OFFER_STOP)).to_s
      return chute if r =~ CHUTE_START
      break if r =~ OFFER_STOP
    end
    say "the justicar said: #{r.strip[0, 160]} -- stopping."
  end

  # still sliding? the last chute line in the recent history isn't the one that ends it
  def self.sliding?
    lines = reget(80, CHUTE_LINES).to_a
    !lines.empty? && lines.last !~ CHUTE_END
  end

  # light from the right/left -> lean that way; straight ahead -> do nothing
  def self.chute
    say "in the chute."
    # a "faint light" prompt that is still the newest chute line came before we started reading
    pending = reget(80, CHUTE_LINES).to_a.last.to_s
    fput "lean #{$1.downcase}" if pending =~ /faint light coming from the (right|left)/i
    deadline = Time.now + 180
    while Time.now < deadline
      line = get?
      unless line
        sleep 0.05
        next
      end
      case line
      when /faint light coming from the (right|left)/i
        fput "lean #{$1.downcase}"
      when /spit out onto the ground/i
        say "out of the chute."
        sleep 1
        return
      end
    end
    say "still in the chute after 3 minutes -- giving up."
  end

  def self.at_loop
    steps = 0
    while where == :loop && steps < 6
      cmd = LOOP_STEP.find { |re, _| descr =~ re }&.last
      unless cmd
        say "can't tell which colored room this is -- walk to the Dead End (orange eye) and run me there."
        return
      end
      say "-> #{cmd} (toward the Dead End)."
      return say("couldn't move #{cmd}.") unless step(cmd)
      steps += 1
    end
    at_dead_end if where == :dead_end
  end

  def self.at_dead_end
    say "Dead End: touching #{RUNES.join(', ')}."
    RUNES.each_with_index do |c, i|
      waitrt?
      fput "touch #{c} rune"
      sleep RUNE_GAP unless i == RUNES.size - 1
    end
    opened = false
    deadline = Time.now + 6
    while Time.now < deadline
      line = get?
      if line.nil?
        sleep 0.1
      elsif line =~ OPENING
        opened = true
        break
      end
    end
    return say("the wall didn't react -- check the runes and run me again.") unless opened
    say "the wall opened -- going through."
    say "couldn't get through the opening." unless step("go opening")
  end

  def self.at_hall
    2.times do
      break unless where == :hall
      say "-> north."
      return say("couldn't go north.") unless step("north")
    end
  end

  # The way on is the trapdoor in this room. Each `jump trapdoor` buckles it a little more but it
  # springs back if you stop for ~20 s (10.26 19:29:10-12, then 19:29:34-37), so jump straight
  # through; 6 jumps did it. (`jump on trapdoor` just says "That was fun.")
  def self.at_grand_first
    say "jumping on the trapdoor until it gives way."
    20.times do
      waitrt?
      r = dothistimeout("jump trapdoor", 3, /buckle|give way|fun\b/i).to_s
      break if r =~ GAVE_WAY
    end
    deadline = Time.now + 4
    sleep 0.2 until where != :grand_first || Time.now > deadline
    say(where == :subterrane ? "dropped into the Subterrane." : "the trapdoor didn't give way.")
  end

  # The north room's door only leads to the Courtyard (a side room, nothing recorded there), and
  # the item is used up, so don't burn it: head back to the trapdoor.
  def self.at_grand_north
    say "this room's door only leads to the Courtyard. The way on is the trapdoor in the room to the south."
    say "couldn't go south." unless step("south")
    at_grand_first if where == :grand_first
  end

  # ---- the way down, from the Subterrane to the Demon Wall ---------------------

  def self.at_subterrane
    say "-> go fissure (the Lich map's command), then north along the Dark Passageway."
    return say("couldn't go through the fissure.") unless step("go fissure")
    at_passage
  end

  def self.at_passage
    6.times do
      break unless where == :passage
      return say("couldn't go north.") unless step("north")
    end
    say "at the abyss; run me again to jump." if where == :abyss_edge
  end

  # leaps into the abyss -> the Void, a safe room where groups wait for each other
  def self.at_abyss
    say "-> jump into the abyss."
    say "didn't land in the Void." unless step("jump")
  end

  # the crevice is found by SEARCHing (Nety "points at a low crevice"); CRAWL goes through one at a time
  def self.at_void
    unless step("crawl crevice")
      say "no crevice yet -- searching."
      waitrt?
      fput "search"
      sleep 2
      return say("couldn't crawl into the crevice.") unless step("crawl crevice")
    end
    at_tunnel
  end

  def self.at_tunnel
    8.times do
      break unless where == :tunnel
      return say("couldn't go down.") unless step("down")
    end
    say "at the Cistern; run me again to SWIM (the hatch locks behind you: no way back up)." if where == :cistern
  end

  def self.at_cistern
    say "-> swim to the hatch (it locks behind you)."
    say "the swim didn't take." unless step("swim", 12)
  end

  def self.at_sunken
    say "-> south, into the Depths."
    return say("couldn't go south.") unless step("south")
    at_depths
  end

  # down while there is a way down (Depths, 4 rooms), then north (3 Deepest Parts, the Palisade)
  def self.at_depths
    14.times do
      break unless where == :depths
      cmd = exits.include?('down') ? 'down' : 'north'
      return say("couldn't go #{cmd}.") unless step(cmd)
    end
    say "at the Demon Wall; run me again to put the ouroboros in its door." if where == :demon_wall
  end

  # ---- Hollowlair ----------------------------------------------------------------

  # The maze shifts and wanders (Nety lost people here), so this only does the one thing that works
  # in the right room: whisper "six" to the heavily carved door (10.26 19:53:58).
  def self.at_dreadgrounds
    unless descr =~ /heavily carved door/i
      return say("not the room with the heavily carved door -- this maze can't be solved by script. Walk until the description mentions it, then run me again.")
    end
    say "whispering to the heavily carved door."
    fput "whisper door six"
    deadline = Time.now + 8
    sleep 0.2 until where != :dreadgrounds || Time.now > deadline
    say "the door didn't answer." if where == :dreadgrounds
  end

  def self.at_sanctuary
    say "-> north, to the Dark Shrine."
    say "couldn't go north." unless step("north")
  end

  # Nety knocked twice and the third time the gate "bursts open, revealing dozens of ethereal
  # tentacles that begin to strangle him": whoever opens it takes that. Unverified verb (the Lich
  # map says GO GATE).
  def self.at_shrine
    3.times do |i|
      say "-> go gate (try #{i + 1} of 3#{i == 2 ? ': this one strangles whoever opens it' : ''})."
      break if step("go gate", 8)
    end
    say "didn't get through the gate." if where == :shrine
  end

  # The fiend is summoned by touching the rune twice; killing it is yours. Its corpse (an
  # "ethereal fiend") is searched for the effigy, which then goes in the barbed stone door.
  def self.at_den(summon)
    fiends = GameObj.npcs.to_a.select { |n| n && n.name.to_s =~ /fiend/i }
    live = fiends.reject { |n| n.status.to_s =~ /dead|gone/ }
    if live.any?
      return say("the fiend is alive -- kill it, then run me again.")
    end
    dead = fiends.find { |n| n.status.to_s =~ /dead|gone/ }
    if dead
      say "searching the dead fiend for the effigy."
      waitrt?
      fput "search ##{dead.id}"
      sleep 1
    elsif GameObj.loot.to_a.none? { |o| o && o.name.to_s =~ /effigy/i } && !holding?(/effigy/i)
      unless summon
        return say("no fiend here. `;son-puz summon` touches the runes twice to call one (you kill it).")
      end
      say "touching the runes twice to call the fiend."
      2.times do
        waitrt?
        fput "touch rune"
        sleep 2
      end
      return
    end
    door
  end

  def self.holding?(re)
    %i[right_hand left_hand].any? { |h| (o = GameObj.send(h)) && o.name.to_s =~ re }
  end

  # ---- the final boss's side ----------------------------------------------------

  def self.at_roost
    say "Demon Roost (a safe room: rest and buff, the boss dispels a lot). -> go gap, up, then the tunnel."
    return say("couldn't go through the gap.") unless step("go gap")
    at_hellscape
  end

  def self.at_hellscape
    4.times do
      case where
      when :hellscape_low  then return say("couldn't go up.") unless step("up")
      when :hellscape_high then return say("couldn't crawl through the tunnel.") unless step("go tunnel", 8)
      else break
      end
    end
    at_church if where == :church
  end

  def self.at_church
    10.times do
      break unless where == :church
      cmd = CHURCH_STEP.find { |re, _| title =~ re }&.last
      return say("don't know the way from #{title.strip}.") unless cmd
      return say("couldn't go #{cmd}.") unless step(cmd)
    end
    say "at the tower. The rune ring round the portal has to be disarmed (Nety did it; it explodes on a failure), then run me again." if where == :tower
  end

  def self.at_tower
    say "-> go portal."
    say "couldn't go through the portal -- is the rune ring still up?" unless step("go portal", 8)
  end

  # GO PATH asks you to confirm within 30 s; the second run of this script is the confirmation
  def self.at_field
    r = dothistimeout("go path", 5, /finite decision|GO path again|You (?:step|walk)|Deeper within/i).to_s
    if r =~ /GO path again/i
      say "that's the point of no return (no way out but the exit or death). Run me again within 30 seconds to go on."
    else
      sleep 1
    end
  end

  # LOOK IN POOL prints "In the pool:" and then "Special [1]: a magical gateway" on the next line
  def self.pool_has_gateway?
    put "look in pool"
    deadline = Time.now + 4
    while Time.now < deadline
      line = get?
      if line.nil?
        sleep 0.05
      elsif line =~ /gateway/i
        return true
      elsif line =~ /nothing in the pool|You see nothing/i
        return false
      end
    end
    false
  end

  def self.at_boss_pool
    unless pool_has_gateway?
      return say("no gateway in the pool yet. Kill the boss (it starts when the sapling is uprooted), search it for the soulstone heart.")
    end
    g = dothistimeout("get heart", 4, /You (?:retrieve|pick up|remove|get|already have)|What were you referring to|could not find|Get what/i).to_s
    if g =~ /What were you referring to|could not find|Get what/i && !holding?(/heart/i)
      return say("no soulstone heart on you or in the room.")
    end
    p = dothistimeout("put heart in gateway", 5, Regexp.union(DOOR_OPENS, /accomplish nothing|What were you referring to|doesn't fit|nothing happens/i)).to_s
    unless p =~ DOOR_OPENS
      return say("the gateway said: #{p.strip[0, 160]} -- stopping (the heart is in your hand).")
    end
    say "gateway open."
    say "the gateway didn't take me through." unless step("go gateway", 8)
  end

  def self.at_veil
    say "The Veil of Solace. `ask monstrosity about reward`, then AS, DS, TD or CS (the same ask twice to confirm). It's permanent, so I won't choose."
  end

  # the door names the shape it wants; get that item, put it in, go through
  def self.door
    r = dothistimeout("look door", 4, /\bdoor\b.*(?:depression|open|closed)/i).to_s
    shape = r[/in the shape of an? (\w+)/i, 1]
    if shape.nil?
      say "no empty depression in the door text (#{r.strip[0, 120]}) -- trying to go through."
      return say("the door didn't take me through.") unless step("go door")
      return
    end
    say "the door wants a #{shape}."
    g = dothistimeout("get #{shape}", 4, /You retrieve|You pick up|You remove|You already have|What were you referring to|could not find|Get what/i).to_s
    if g =~ /What were you referring to|could not find|Get what/i
      say "no #{shape} on you or in the room. Kill things (the drops are your puzzle items), `look` on the floor for it, then run me again."
      return
    end
    p = dothistimeout("put #{shape} in door", 5, Regexp.union(DOOR_OPENS, /accomplish nothing|What were you referring to|doesn't fit|nothing happens/i)).to_s
    unless p =~ DOOR_OPENS
      say "the door said: #{p.strip[0, 160]} -- stopping (the #{shape} is in your hand)."
      return
    end
    say "door open."
    say "the door didn't take me through." unless step("go door")
  end

  def self.at_courtyard
    say "Courtyard: a side room (a fountain, gravestones, a mural of Old One Eye; the only exit is the door you came in by). The way on is the trapdoor in the Grand Hall's first room: -> back out and south."
    return say("couldn't go back through the door.") unless step("go door")
    at_grand_north if where == :grand_door
  end

  def self.run(arg)
    pay, summon = arg == 'pay', arg == 'summon'
    return chute if sliding?
    spot = where
    return say("don't recognize this room (#{title.strip}) -- stand in a Sonreeva or Hollowlair room, the mausoleum door, or the Mausoleum.") unless spot
    say "at #{spot}."
    case spot
    when :mausoleum_door then at_mausoleum_door
    when :mausoleum      then at_mausoleum(pay)
    when :loop           then at_loop
    when :dead_end       then at_dead_end
    when :hall           then at_hall
    when :grand_first    then at_grand_first
    when :grand_door     then at_grand_north
    when :dais           then door
    when :courtyard      then at_courtyard
    when :subterrane     then at_subterrane
    when :passage        then at_passage
    when :abyss_edge     then at_abyss
    when :void           then at_void
    when :tunnel         then at_tunnel
    when :cistern        then at_cistern
    when :sunken         then at_sunken
    when :depths         then at_depths
    when :demon_wall     then door
    when :dreadgrounds   then at_dreadgrounds
    when :sanctuary      then at_sanctuary
    when :shrine         then at_shrine
    when :den            then at_den(summon)
    when :roost          then at_roost
    when :hellscape_low, :hellscape_high then at_hellscape
    when :church         then at_church
    when :tower          then at_tower
    when :field          then at_field
    when :boss_pool      then at_boss_pool
    when :veil           then at_veil
    end
    say "done at #{where || 'somewhere new'}."
  end
end

SonPuz.run(script.vars[1].to_s.downcase)
